134 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 94 0 R/E(The International Press Corps, or the media, is known to serve as the guardian to protect the unbiased truth and is thus hailed as the fourth pillar of democracy. The committee embodies a vital international platform tasked to constantly monitor and question the government and various organisations. Its purpose is to broadcast and disseminate information about current affairs in politics, economy, culture, and society thus shaping public opinion on events and issues that are of global significance.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

135 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 94 0 R/E(Despite such challenges, it has become a need of the hour to minimise the erosion of journalistic ethics, so that the Press Corps can serve the purpose of becoming the people's voice, as the press corps must remain the  watchdog of the global establishments, and not their loyal pet.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

136 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 94 0 R/T(To uphold their role as global media, freedom of the press becomes a fundamental liberty for its existence, which has now been jeopardized due to several factors, including the emergence of biased and sensationalized "yellow journalism". Other factors include government and public hostility towards members of the press, media manipulation by propagandists, state-sanctioned restrictions to access information, lack of protection, and threats to their lives.)/E(To uphold their role as global media, freedom of the press becomes a fundamental liberty for its existence, which has now been jeopardized due to several factors, including the emergence of biased and sensationalized "yellow journalism". Other factors include government and public hostility towards members of the press, media manipulation by propagandists, state-sanctioned restrictions to access information, lack of protection, and threats to their lives.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

