<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 101 0 R/E(FROM THE EYE OF HYPOCRISY!)/Pg 17 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

319 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 101 0 R/E( - The New York Times)/Pg 17 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

320 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 101 0 R/E(The floor today of the United Nations Commission on the Status of Women found itself engulfed in rugged dialogue amongst its delegates. The council's atmosphere was charged with serious deliberations and discord, with no delegate willing to support the claims of the other, but only keeping forward their points.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

321 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 101 0 R/E(The day began under bleak weather, mirroring the sombre atmosphere of the chambers of the UNCSW. The committee proceedings went forward with the delegate of the Republic of India successfully proposing a motion to suspend formal debate and raise a moderated caucus addressing the financial challenges confronted by women from marginalized Islamic communities. The subsequent moderate rated caucus revolved around the tension between Middle Eastern and Islamic nations vis-\340-vis Western nations. To spread the flames of condemnation, the delegate of the United States of America with her unwavering courage and a gutsy speech, denounced Middle Eastern countries for their alleged hypocrisy, highlighting the irony of these nations lecturing Western countries on gendered Islamophobia, but at the same time lack)/Pg 17 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

322 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 101 0 R/E(neglecting serious violation of human rights against their own female citizens. They fiercely exposed the of initiative of the countries of the Middle East in making efforts to help women get civil rights.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

323 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 101 0 R/E(Taking the same argument forward, a guest speaker further intensified the condemnation by accusing the Republic of Pakistan of espousing Muslim laws from the Quran that promote intolerance towards other religions, yet at the same time denouncing Western intolerance towards Muslims.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

324 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 101 0 R/E(Amidst this verbal exchange, the delegate of Afghanistan attempted to redirect all the blame toward the Western countries, specifically pointing out France for having an enormous Muslim population, yet having a perceived lack of efforts to make them feel included. However, their appeal remained undercut as the delegate of Afghanistan failed to mention any wrongdoings on their side.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

325 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 101 0 R/E(Despite the exchange of rhetoric and accusations between these historic adversaries, hopes for the committee's progress remained elusive with the committee at large failing to deliver practical speeches on showcase tangible efforts from the respective nations. Consequently, In such such a scenario- the entire proceedings of the moderated caucus yielded little real benefit.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

