397 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 104 0 R/E("The media's the most powerful entity on earth. They have the power to make the innocent guilty and to make the guilty innocent, and that's power. Because they control the minds of the masses." Malcolm X)/Pg 20 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

398 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 104 0 R/E(To have to reiterate the impact of mass media and journalism on society would be a piece of great inanity, given its universality across the world in different nations, governments, and unions. While a free and unbiased press is integral to democracy, the press, in many 'democratic countries has often been suffocated, censored, or manipulated.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

399 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 104 0 R/E(A 2021 Pew Research Center report showed that American adults' trust in National News Organizations dropped from 76% to 58% between 2016 and 2021. Another study indicated that journalists in the USA in comparison to the public, were more likely to believe that not all sides always deserve equal coverage. What caused this shift? Has media bias always existed, or has it recently worsened?)/Pg 20 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

400 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 104 0 R/E(The answers to all those questions are not as modest as they may seem, for propaganda and misinformation go beyond what is written in a dictionary, for they are rooted in history, where the politics of fear has driven conquests far and beyond. Media bias has existed historically, often used to propel propaganda for one side and misinformation for the other, with motivations ranging from strategic alliances to in-cash settlements, all brought in to propel more propaganda.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

401 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 104 0 R/E(Biased media narratives are more likely seen being produced in countries, with more authoritative, and centralized government systems, which may also see powerful individuals associated with [at times, against] the government owning or controlling media outlets, and their output.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

402 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 104 0 R/E(In a disturbing trend, Reporters Without Borders \(RSF\) noted that 26 out of 31 Asian countries saw a decline in press freedom on their 2024 annual index, with no Asia-Pacific country in the top 15. Authoritative regimes have emerged in many of these countries, trend gaining momentum in parts of Europe over the past decade.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

