443 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(Like in the game of chess, the two sides of diplomatic relations are world war and world peace. While the latter belongs to Team White, the former represents Team Black. While Team White always plays the move of diplomacy, Team Black always tends to play the move of misconduct. Every war that has ever been started around the world has been viewed as a blatant diplomatic failure in which nations were checkmated.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

444 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(In one such prominent case, during the time of the "Mahabharata," Shri Krishna arrived at the palace of the astute King Dhritarashtra, the father of the 'Kauravas' in Hastinapur with a proposal formulated by Shri Krishna himself on behalf of the Pandavas who had gone on an exile for a period of 12 years as an act of defeat after losing a dice game in which they also forfeited their capital, "Indraprastha" along with their other belongings.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

445 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(Since King Dhritarashtra Dhr was regarded as the trustee of righteousness, Shri Krishna appealed to him and tried to persuade him of the seriousness of the consequences if peace was not restored. The two groups of cousins from the same family, the "Kauravas" and "Pandavas," were at odds because the former was jealous of the latter's success and happiness.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

446 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(He also discussed the aftermath of a war, saying that even though one side wins and the other loses, both sides suffer proportionately large losses, but the universe as a whole would be harmoniously restored once peace had been restored. Duryodhan, however, strongly objected to Shri Krishna's diplomatic ploy and rejected the peace proposal. To give the Pandavas one last chance, Shri Krishna humbly asked King Dhritarashtra to lend them only five villages: Avishthala, Vrikasthala, Makandi, Varanavata, and any others for the fifth.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

447 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 106 0 R/E(This action by Shri Krishna even enraged Duryodhan, who then tried to humiliate Shri Krishna and kidnap him. This ultimately resulted in the massive and significant "Battle of Kurukshetra," where the "Pandavas" restored their glory at the expense of their loved ones and the "Kauravas" lost everything. To ensure that World Peace, Human Rights, Justice, and Equality prevail in the world undisturbed and allow mankind to flourish, the concept of "diplomacy" is important. If wars didn't occur, it would wreak havoc everywhere.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

